# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS NEEDED
#   core.autocrlf=true is set in the *global* git config (it is not in
#   .git/config), and until now this repo had no .gitattributes. That means
#   every fresh clone or checkout rewrote LF -> CRLF, which silently breaks
#   files that are not consumed by a Windows text editor:
#     backend/Dockerfile ......... CMD ["sh", "-c", "..."] gains a trailing CR
#     docker-compose.yml ......... YAML scalars gain a trailing CR
#     backend/.env.example ...... dotenv readers (limits / starlette) return
#     backend/ratelimit.env ..... values ending with CR, e.g. DB_HOST=127.0.0.1\r
#     *.sh ...................... bash: "bad interpreter" / "command not found\r"
#   .gitattributes has higher precedence than core.autocrlf, so these rules win
#   regardless of each developer's local setting.
#
# NO RENORMALIZATION COMMIT IS REQUIRED
#   All 566 tracked blobs are already stored with LF (verified with
#   `git ls-files --eol`: 561 i/lf, 4 binary, 1 empty). The clean filter below
#   turns a CRLF working copy back into the same LF blob, so `git status` stays
#   clean after adding this file.

* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files that must be LF: assert it explicitly instead of relying on the
# text/binary heuristic, so a future editor cannot flip them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.py    text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.vue   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.ini   text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
*.env           text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Windows-only inputs keep CRLF.
#   Batch files are parsed by cmd.exe, which mishandles LF-only labels/goto.
#   Start.txt is the human quick-start note opened in Notepad.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
/Start.txt text eol=crlf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never run the EOL filters on binary content.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.zip    binary
*.docx   binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.pptx   binary
*.pdf    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.webp   binary
*.bmp    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.eot    binary
*.jar    binary
*.db     binary
*.sqlite binary
*.pyc    binary
